  "full_text": "Can I sit here? Yes. No, I'm not. Go ahead. But your Bible back here, it was up in the sun. Okay. I keep telling Mom. It's not right up here. Yeah. Forever discontent. Beware, be under guard against every form of greed, for not even when one has an abundance does his life consist of his possessions. Let's take a brief look at greed. Practically speaking, greed is an inordinate desire for more. an excessive, unsatisfied hunger to possess. Like an untamed beast, greed grasps, claws, clutches, reaches, and clings, stubbornly refusing to surrender. The word enough is not in this beast's vocabulary. Akin to envy and jealousy, greed is nevertheless distinct. Envy wants to have what someone else possesses. Jealousy wants to possess what it already has. But greed is different. Greed is forever discontent and therefore is insatiably craving, longing, wanting, striving for more and more and more. That's the whole point of greed. You want more and more of something that really isn't good for you. And in the getting of it, you'll suffer the painful consequences. That's why Jesus warns, beware, be on your guard. This thing is like a cancer, an insatiable leech that will suck the life right out of you. Enough will never be enough. Beware.",
